NVD GLMsingle Type-D derivatives

The model jointly fits all 33 task runs for each participant (s1-s11 across
three physical sessions) using GLMsingle at official commit
1ab54a65edd3ea41a6133d4b4ecb78a9c7296684. The model selects HRFs, noise PCs and
fractional ridge regularization, with autoscaling and percent-signal-change
betas. The original fMRIPrep StartTime is subtracted from event onsets before
nearest-TR design binning. The leading BIDS session-label digit identifies
physical sessions for cross-validation; rest is excluded.

rawBetasmd means trial estimates before condition averaging; it remains a
denoised/regularized Type-D result. Every run CIFTI scalar is paired with the
same row in its TSV. avgBetasmd is an arithmetic mean grouped by explicit
condition/image ID across the actual recorded presentations, with each count
reported in the TSV. It does not presume exactly three repeats.

VisualROIs maps keep the complete original 91282-grayordinate BrainModelAxis
and set voxels/vertices outside the selected visual ROIs or subject fit mask
to NaN. ROI membership is remapped from HCP-MMP1.0 atlas hemisphere+surface
vertex IDs into the actual fMRIPrep axis. metadata/ contains ROI IDs, vertex
correspondence, full ROI map and both zero/one-based grayordinate indices.

The betas suffix, avg/ and metadata/ are documented NVD project extensions.
Data remain derivatives, not raw BOLD; scalar beta indices are not timepoints.
Sources and all metadata use public BIDS URIs rather than private HPC paths.
Work files, pickle checkpoints, local paths, licenses and credentials are
excluded. Source: OpenNeuro ds007354 snapshot 2.0.5, CC0.
